(a) The clean city commission shall recommend refuse and environmental management policies to the mayor and council in order that all city refuse, beautification and other clean city activities may follow a common purpose. The clean city commission shall have the following responsibilities:
(1) Develop city-wide refuse and environmental recommendations;
(2) Determine and recommend to the mayor and council program priorities on a city-wide basis;
(3) Recommend enforcement and additional program alternatives;
(4) Study city performance from data collected and examined under the Keep America Beautiful, Inc., Clean City Council;
(5) Encourage and plan landscaping, planting and/or preservation of trees, flowers, plants, shrubs and other objects or ornamentations;
(6) Carry out such other tasks as the council may designate.
(b) To accomplish the responsibilities outlined in subsection (a) of this section, the clean city commission may establish subcommittees including, but not limited to, the areas of business and industry, communications, community organizations, municipal operations, schools, finance and recycling. Each subcommittee will be chaired by a clean city commission member with a number of community volunteers established and chosen by the clean city commission, a working subcommittee staff.
(Code 1977, § 2-86)
